  "headline": "Government Officials Deny Presidential Advice Regarding Legal Case",
  "seoTitle": "Officials Deny Presidential Advice in Gibran Diploma Dispute",
  "metaDescription": "Government communications officials clarify that the President did not advise the Vice President to pursue legal action regarding diploma disputes.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Head of Indonesian Government Communications Syahganda Nainggolan denied claims that President Prabowo advised Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka to contest diploma issues in court.",
    "Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka previously stated an intention to pursue legal action at the Administrative Court (PTUN) to verify his high school diploma.",
    "Legal observers and government officials maintain that existing decisions from the Constitutional Court and Supreme Court regarding the matter are final."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "A public debate has emerged regarding the legal status of Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka's academic credentials. The Vice President expressed an intention to challenge the validity of his high school diploma through the Administrative Court (PTUN) and suggested that President Prabowo Subianto had provided advice on the matter, likening the President's role to a father figure. However, the Head of the Indonesian Government Communications Agency, Syahganda Nainggolan, officially denied that the President offered such counsel or suggested legal confrontation. Meanwhile, Coordinating Minister Yusril Ihza Mahendra reaffirmed that previous rulings from the Constitutional Court and the Supreme Court are legally binding and final. Legal analysts have voiced criticism regarding the Vice President's plan, suggesting that attempting to relitigate the matter via the PTUN contradicts established judicial outcomes and advocating for resignation as an alternative approach.",
